<style>
  body {
    font-family: 'Segoe UI', Calibri, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 11pt;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: #1e293b;
    margin: 30px;
  }
  .header-card {
    background-color: #0f172a;
    color: #ffffff;
    padding: 24px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 25px;
    border-left: 8px solid #2563eb;
  }
  .header-title {
    font-size: 20pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #38bdf8;
    margin: 0 0 6px 0;
  }
  .header-sub {
    font-size: 13pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #f8fafc;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
  }
  .header-desc {
    font-size: 10pt;
    color: #cbd5e1;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .rules-card {
    background-color: #f0fdf4;
    border: 2.5px solid #16a34a;
    padding: 18px 22px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    margin-bottom: 30px;
  }
  .rules-title {
    font-size: 13pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #15803d;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .rule-item {
    font-size: 10.5pt;
    color: #0f172a;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  .rule-num {
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #16a34a;
    background-color: #dcfce7;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    margin-right: 8px;
  }
  .group-title {
    font-size: 13.5pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #0f172a;
    margin-top: 25px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    padding-bottom: 4px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #cbd5e1;
  }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  th {
    background-color: #1e293b;
    color: #ffffff;
    font-weight: bold;
    padding: 10px 12px;
    text-align: left;
    font-size: 10pt;
    border: 1px solid #0f172a;
  }
  td {
    padding: 8px 12px;
    border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;
    font-size: 9.5pt;
    vertical-align: middle;
  }
  tr:nth-child(even) {
    background-color: #f8fafc;
  }
  .code-badge {
    font-weight: bold;
    font-size: 10.5pt;
    color: #ffffff;
    background-color: #2563eb;
    padding: 3px 8px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    text-align: center;
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .keyword-badge {
    font-family: Consolas, 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-weight: bold;
    font-size: 9pt;
    color: #0369a1;
    background-color: #e0f2fe;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid #bae6fd;
  }
  .file-name {
    font-family: Consolas, 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 9pt;
    color: #475569;
    background-color: #f1f5f9;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
  .footer {
    margin-top: 40px;
    padding-top: 15px;
    border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
    font-size: 9pt;
    color: #64748b;
    text-align: center;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="header-card">
  <div class="header-title">INTERNATIONAL CONSORTIUM OF JURISTS (ICJ)</div>
  <div class="header-sub">7 गोल्डन इंजीनियरिंग नियम एवं मास्टर मॉड्यूल कोड डायरेक्टरी</div>
  <div class="header-desc">
    Official Scope Isolation, Stability & Architectural Protection Codebook Specification • 2026
  </div>
</div>

<div class="rules-card">
  <div class="rules-title">🛡️ 7 गोल्डन इंजीनियरिंग नियम (7 Mandatory Engineering Rules):</div>
  <div class="rule-item"><span class="rule-num">1</span> <strong>Every development request should identify the target module Code whenever possible.</strong></div>
  <div class="rule-item"><span class="rule-num">2</span> <strong>Use the System Keyword as the stable English identifier for the module.</strong></div>
  <div class="rule-item"><span class="rule-num">3</span> <strong>Modify only the existing architecture and files relevant to the selected Code.</strong></div>
  <div class="rule-item"><span class="rule-num">4</span> <strong>Do not create duplicate frontend sections, modules, services or data-entry points when existing functionality can be reused.</strong></div>
  <div class="rule-item"><span class="rule-num">5</span> <strong>Do not modify unrelated Codes/modules.</strong></div>
  <div class="rule-item"><span class="rule-num">6</span> <strong>After changes, run the relevant build/validation checks.</strong></div>
  <div class="rule-item"><span class="rule-num">7</span> <strong>Do not expose secrets, passwords, API keys or other sensitive credentials in source code or UI.</strong></div>
</div>

